# Cursor Rules — aws-log-anomaly-mlops

## Task Tracking
- ALWAYS read TASKS.md before starting any task
- ALWAYS update TASKS.md by marking completed items [x] after finishing them
- NEVER mark an item [x] unless the file was actually created and is non-empty
- After every response, show the current state of the relevant TASKS.md section
- If a task is partially done, leave it [ ] and add a comment next to it: <!-- in progress -->

## Code Standards
- All Terraform resources must have a `description` in every variable block
- All Terraform resources must have a `tags` block with: Project, Environment, ManagedBy
- All Python scripts must include logging using the `logging` module, not print statements
- All IAM policies must follow least-privilege — no wildcard `*` on actions unless unavoidable
- No hardcoded AWS account IDs, ARNs, or credentials anywhere — use variables or secrets

## File Structure
- Terraform files live in `terraform/` only
- SageMaker Pipeline definition lives in `pipeline/` only
- Training scripts live in `training/` only
- Inference scripts live in `inference/` only
- GitHub Actions workflows live in `.github/workflows/` only

## GitHub Actions
- Always use OIDC for AWS authentication — never use static AWS_ACCESS_KEY_ID/SECRET
- Always pin action versions (e.g. actions/checkout@v4, not actions/checkout@latest)
- Always set `permissions` block explicitly on every job

## Terraform
- Always use HCP Terraform (app.terraform.io) as the remote state backend
- Always run in this order: fmt → validate → plan → apply
- Never use `terraform destroy` without a `-target` flag in CI

## AWS Region
- Default region is ca-central-1 unless explicitly told otherwise

## When Unsure
- Ask before creating a file that is not in TASKS.md
- Ask before modifying a file that was already marked [x] in TASKS.md
